Subject: ncrypt: upstream ECDSA keys + persisted keys (NCryptOpenKey, named NCryptCreatePersistedKey, NCryptDeleteKey)
Upstream Wine dlls/ncrypt (wine-mirror master 2026-10-29), ported as a whole: 0a13e4af4b + f0d380f2ba ECDSA
P256/P384/P521, 4404cd751b common object header, 62d82e3761 algorithm group, 2020261203 + 4426edc42a NCryptImportKey
params/data (Hans Leidekker); 6f0403ada5 + f16ee9c3ea refcounted provider handles (Piotr Caban); c30414f652 +
dc3e79b425 NCryptEncrypt/NCryptDecrypt padding (Hans Leidekker). ncrypt_internal.h folded into main.c as upstream.
Added here (not upstream): persisted keys of the software KSP stored in the prefix registry
(HKCU/HKLM Software\Wine\NCrypt\UserKeys|MachineKeys\<name>: private blob + algorithm), NCryptOpenKey loads
them (NTE_BAD_KEYSET when missing), NCryptCreatePersistedKey returns NTE_EXISTS without NCRYPT_OVERWRITE_KEY_FLAG,
NCryptFinalizeKey stores, NCryptDeleteKey removes. Why: the Epic Online Services SDK (Epic Games Launcher) keeps its
DPoP key "Epic/EpicGamesLauncher/EOS/Auth" (ECDSA_P256) this way; without it EOS login failed (GenerateDpop failed
to parse public key -> EOS_NotConfigured) and account linking returned 400. LGPL-2.1.

